-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:16:48Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-09-24T21:12:32Z","updated_at":"2026-09-27T01:01:58Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123811","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123811","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123811.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123811.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #123723\r\n\r\nFixes a crash due to the EngineDebugger being NULL when the editor is not present.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nAdded a check to see if the EngineDebugger is available before using it in the embedded macOS display server. The crash can occur if Godot is ran with the --embedded flag on macOS without the editor present. The scenario from the linked issue will still end in a crash due to a separate bug that results in not cleaning up the engine when the embedded macOS display server fails to be created, so I have added a second commit to fix that bug too in order to fix the linked issue without any crashes.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123811/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123811/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}